thub.com/users/enginsoysal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"text/plain; charset=utf-8","state":"uploaded","size":1856,"digest":"sha256:95edd24b9779c9639ed0f56dffb5f02343c0459b9833564ffa592aef5a4730a4","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-11-18T18:51:06Z","updated_at":"2026-11-18T18:51:06Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/releases/download/m1311-v0.13.11/M13STAGE11-SHA256SUMS.txt"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/releases/assets/764576511","id":764576511,"node_id":"RA_kwDOVj6ISs4tkoL_","name":"m13stage11-starter-manifest.json","label":"","uploader":{"login":"enginsoysal","id":103884748,"node_id":"U_kgDOBjEnzA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/103884748?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal","html_url":"https://github.com/enginsoysal","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/json","state":"uploaded","size":656,"digest":"sha256:75c520c3eac5aadd615ef7d59d0532aa9eae5d9f2462b223c934a273128b5415","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-11-18T18:51:07Z","updated_at":"2026-11-18T18:51:07Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/releases/download/m1311-v0.13.11/m13stage11-starter-manifest.json"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/tarball/m1311-v0.13.11","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/zipball/m1311-v0.13.11","body":"# Engacer OS M13.11 / 0.13.11 - Personalization and optional screensaver\n\nExact native qualification passes M13-STAGE11-VM-v1. This is a scoped testing release; matching public website delivery is a separate closure gate. Stability investigation remains exclusively M13.13, after M13.12 integration.\n\nUse the [matching installation guide](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/6c8d0d7d6f61ae1b03470680659e05f296076ae5/docs/handbook/install-m1311.md), [personalization and screensaver guide](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/6c8d0d7d6f61ae1b03470680659e05f296076ae5/docs/handbook/personalization-m1311.md), [Settings search guide](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/6c8d0d7d6f61ae1b03470680659e05f296076ae5/docs/handbook/settings-m1311.md) and [Start guide](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/6c8d0d7d6f61ae1b03470680659e05f296076ae5/docs/handbook/start-m136.md).\n\n## Exact media\n\n- Build: `61034b7befcf6135226d034f0c437d28`.\n- ISO SHA256: `60b894d7ce5c251641794b9d0fa047762b2b8b9d718468af9062949a5e73fdc8`.\n- VMware ZIP SHA256: `898960cec8ec36a7ca5dfcdcadcbdb1a258e6beefcd0dab90ec44c1d29dd323b`.\n\nThe exact starter contains a new blank growable 20-GiB SATA disk, two CPUs, 128 MiB RAM, UEFI and Secure Boot off. All shipped devices remain enabled; the disk is not preinstalled and firmware boot order is not forced. Extract the whole ZIP and open EngacerOS.vmx.\n\n## What changes\n\nSettings → Appearance adds the optional Off-by-default Screensaver page. Choose one, five or ten actual idle minutes and the native Engacer logo, Clock or Blank style. Preview never saves; Apply persists a strict separate twenty-byte per-user record. Cancel, leaving the page or closing restores the saved choices, and a competing Settings window cannot replace another owner's draft.\n\nThe saver reuses the existing buffers, renderer, timer wakeups and physical input providers. It adds no worker or framebuffer. Reduced motion keeps the logo still; Clock uses the shared UTC service independently of the optional Clock app. Physical key holds and genuine input changes are tracked separately from translated keys and periodic zero-motion reports. Preview waits for its activating gesture to finish; wake consumes the entire first gesture before returning to retained windows and dirty work.\n\nHigh contrast gains an explicit white Start perimeter and current Files-place boundary. Existing appearance, accessibility, Start, taskbar and optional-app choices keep their independent validated data. Every recipe defaults the saver to Off; no unsupported schema-3 preference field or system-file data-package target is offered.\n\n## Qualification scope\n\nThe declared functional matrix includes five native control/display profiles, actual Settings transactions and optional-app independence, saver styles/ownership/wake, one real minute of idle activation, malformed-record refusal, physical 4K and compact theme/readability checks, bounded resource deltas and exact enabled-device VMware installation/independent startups with visible RFB preview/wake. [Exact native acceptance](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/6c8d0d7d6f61ae1b03470680659e05f296076ae5/evidence/M13/11/acceptance-results.json) passes 62 native checks, four VMware checks and 57 declared app-frame captures across 613 compiled inputs. [Resources](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/6c8d0d7d6f61ae1b03470680659e05f296076ae5/evidence/M13/11/resources.json) record fixed desktop state of 557516 bytes (+112), physical-input module BSS +76 bytes including alignment, unchanged installer state and font masks, and zero retention in the measured completed tasks. Independent stopped-image semantic cases do not make a within-session retention claim.\n\nThe one-minute idle task qualifies timeout behavior, not stability. Long-duration use, historical natural-freeze reproduction and reset-chain diagnosis remain M13.13. Whole-product controller and original MSI application integration follow in M13.12. General Windows compatibility, vendor GPU 3D, physical-device universality and a human novice study are not claimed.\n\nThe optional screensaver does not authenticate users, lock the computer or control display power. Off disables automatic presentation. Personal documents, app packages and the existing appearance record remain independent.\n\n## Initial candidate correction\n\nThe unqualified ec856eaf candidate is withdrawn: its cursor-free saver branch skipped the normal graphics presentation flush, so VMware remained on Settings despite an active saver in RAM. The corrected build explicitly presents the existing damage without drawing a cursor. Exact visible VMware Preview/wake and two independent starts pass; the complete declared functional matrix also passes fresh on these corrected bytes. This adds no framebuffer, retained state, mode change or stability experiment. Original failures and the stopped owned-RAM input observations remain documented in the [stage record](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/6c8d0d7d6f61ae1b03470680659e05f296076ae5/docs/milestones/m13-11.md).\n\n## Licensing\n\nOriginal project contributions retain MIT licensing. Included third-party components keep their notices and corresponding license/source assets. The matching release contains twenty complete assets and exact checksums after qualification.\n"}